A||N||2||beachbomb||Cruise control questions!||||5||
Z||000000||beachbomb||01-31-2001||06:04 PM||||Hey all, I have a '84 Indy, the cruise hasn't worked since i bought it,(and to be honest i haven't really tried to trouble shoot it yet. My question is, is there some basic things i should check first before really getting into it. I did replaced all vacuum hoses in engine compatment a while back. PLease help!..Thanks!! Jim(2 '84 Indys) ||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||02-01-2001||01:01 PM||||Well, you could start by checking to see if the fuse is blown.  Then, might try setting the cruise control while you pull up on the brake (and/or clutch pedal) with your toe. <P>You asked for basic stuff - !  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||02-01-2001||01:41 PM||||There are a couple of safety switches down on your pedals.  One on the clutch to keep the engine from revving up when the clutch is disengaged and one on the brake to keep your cruise from trying to speed up the car when you're trying to slow it down.  Mine are made out of milky white plastic.  Those tend to go bad and won't allow your CC to work.  The one on my clutch was worn out.  I took it apart and fixed it, but the metal is fatigued so I'm waiting for it to fail again.<p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 02-01-2001).]||||reg||1
